  "question": {
    "text": "A line passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math> are non-negative integers, on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> lies at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math> units, from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. The distance between the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>A line passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So, the equation of line will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, the direction cosines will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><msqrt><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msqrt><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mstyle></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>3</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msqrt><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>≡</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>7</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>3</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>7</mn></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, given point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math> from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>So, by using the equation of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>21</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the distance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>324</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn></math></p>"
  }
}